  "id": "COMPOUND:32420 - PROTEIN:4699",
  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is implicated in the activation of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase kinase 3 through a series of molecular interactions involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C acts as a target for Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn activates the kinase cascade leading to the final target. This pathway is consistently supported by high scores in the three visible paths, indicating a robust mechanistic link. The shared involvement of Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a mediator across different targets underscores a potential common mechanism, possibly involving the regulation of kinase activity. The presence of a single, well-defined pathway across multiple paths strengthens the hypothesis, though the exact nature of the interaction between Oblonganoside C and Ent-Gloeosteretriol remains to be elucidated. The integration of these findings supports a role for this compound in modulating the MAP3K3 signaling pathway, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise mechanism of action.",
